+- Remaining risks or follow-ups
+  - Slow-query threshold is currently the store default (`250ms`) with constructor options for tests/embedders; no runtime config key was added in this story.
+  - `QueryRow` duration is measured through `Scan`, which is the point where pgx surfaces the result/error for single-row calls.
+- **Learnings for future iterations:**
+  - Store wrappers that forward a `sql string` parameter to pgx must be included in the SQL-injection static-test passthrough exemption; repository call sites remain the real SQL-constant enforcement boundary.
